places.tsv and cells.tsv (the offline place data of the Compartments persona) contain data from these sources.

- GeoNames, https://www.geonames.org/, "cities15000" (cities with at least 15000 inhabitants), licensed under Creative
  Commons Attribution 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). places.tsv keeps, per city, the GeoNames
  identifier, the name, the country, the coordinates rounded to 0.00001 degree and the time zone. It adds the mobile
  country code of the country. Cities that lie beyond 80 degrees of latitude, that have no cell data in their country
  or whose name has a control character were left out.

- Cell tower data from OpenCelliD, https://opencellid.org/, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). cells.tsv is adapted material: only LTE cells were kept, each
  of the country's mobile network code that lies within 25 km of a city was listed for that city, nearest to the
  city centre first, at most 20 per city; the radio type, the coordinates, the range, the sample count and every other
  column were removed. cells.tsv is shared under the same
  licence, CC BY-SA 4.0. The rest of the image is not part of this adaptation.

The files say which cell identities and which time zone belong to a city in this data. They are not a map of the world.
